<p>President Trump launched U.S. military strikes on Iran. The strikes set off explosions in Tehran and immediately sparked a political and legal fight in Washington over whether the Constitution requires Congress to authorize entry into such hostilities. On Capitol Hill, most Republicans backed the president’s decision. Democrats — along with a small number of Republicans — argued Congress must vote, and moved to invoke the 1973 War Powers Act to constrain or end the operation without approval. The debate is also spilling into Trump’s political base: some MAGA-aligned voices say the strike breaks promises to avoid new foreign wars, even as party leaders and foreign-policy hawks rallied behind the action.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/x98C8Y0LBqN1djfUcLf-JFY_GpYzCHLvmdVQkgr8dRSMz-FOkL-P4pUocvaw2cgmHgF795qZo8fMC1ioXJo8voA5AXNw8yLf3BjivzkLdvdJloi9ESnn_5wQd0FSfHwW2rKsfs3CHj9A0KsnI3Y-E_Pg8zOO3cdYl6TIjCKYEgHmdvu0SJU' alt='President Trump described the Iran attack as “major combat operations” that could result in American casualties.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>War powers votes: Rep. Ro Khanna and Rep. Thomas Massie pressed to bring the House back to vote on their authorization bill, while Sen. Tim Kaine urged the Senate to return and vote on his resolution to restrict U.S. forces in Iran without approval.</li><li>Executive-branch dominance: Semafor said the strikes underscored how much war-making authority Congress has ceded, with key Republican leaders signaling little interest in checking a campaign described as aiming at regime change.</li><li>Democratic message: Democrats are trying to argue Trump is choosing a new war over affordability, with Sen. Andy Kim saying voters see Trump as “wildly out of sync with the American people”.</li><li>Election framing: Democratic strategists and lawmakers are looking to frame the Iran operation as an echo of the Iraq war era — and as a political liability for Trump heading into 2026, Semafor reported.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Sen. Lindsey Graham: Graham, a Trump ally, said the operation would be &quot;violent, extensive and I believe, at the end of the day, successful,&quot; according to CBS News. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-strikes-trump-administration-united-states-lawmakers/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Rep. Thomas Massie: Massie called the strikes &quot;acts of war unauthorized by Congress&quot; in comments cited by Semafor. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/28/2026/trump-sidelines-republican-congress-on-iran-strikes'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Political risk and public opinion: The Christian Science Monitor said the strikes carry political risk because Congress did not vote on them, and because public opinion has been opposed to military action in Iran. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Politics/2026/0228/trump-iran-congress-america-first'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li><li>Antiwar MAGA wing: Al Jazeera reported that conservative antiwar opposition exists but remains limited, while Republican hawks praised Trump’s decision to strike Iran. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/1/despite-antiwar-maga-wing-trump-gets-republican-support-for-iran-strikes'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/28/2026/democrats-see-iraq-echoes-in-trumps-iran-war'>Democrats see Iraq echoes in Trump’s Iran war</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/28/world/middleeast/trump-iran-war-powers.html'>Trump’s Unilateral Iran Strike Sparks Constitutional War Powers Dispute</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633270-us-congress-split-strikes-iran/'>Unauthorized war or justified action? US Congress split on Iran strikes</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/usa/2026-03-01/the-attack-on-iran-opens-a-rift-in-the-maga-world-for-trump.html'>The attack on Iran opens a rift in the MAGA world for Trump</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/1/despite-antiwar-maga-wing-trump-gets-republican-support-for-iran-strikes'>Despite antiwar MAGA wing, Trump gets Republican support for Iran strikes</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-strikes-trump-administration-united-states-lawmakers/'>U.S. politicians react after Trump launches military operation against Iran</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Politics/2026/0228/trump-iran-congress-america-first'>Congress didn’t authorize Iran strikes. Trump’s move to do so carries political risks.</a> - csmonitor.com</li></ul>